Subject: [PATCH] OSCORE: restore the replay state when verification fails

Defect: coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu() advances
the Recipient Context replay window before verification. On a countersignature
failure it never rolled back (requests and responses), on an AEAD failure only
requests were rolled back, and oscore_roll_back_seq() skips saved values of 0
and does not restore initial_state. A forged group message with a fresh PIV
could therefore push the window forward, so the genuine message with that PIV
was then rejected as a replay.

Group OSCORE Sections 7.2 / 7.4: if the signature verification fails the
recipient "SHALL NOT update the Replay Window"; RFC 8613 Sections 8.2 Step 6 /
8.4 Step 5: the window is updated only after successful decryption.

Save the replay state (last_seq, sliding_window, initial_state) just before
this message changes it and restore exactly that state on a signature or
decryption failure. Nothing is restored unless this message saved it.
Requests processed with COAP_OSCORE_DECRYPT_NO_REPLAY save nothing.

Applies on top of 0005.
---
--- a/src/coap_oscore.c
+++ b/src/coap_oscore.c
@@ -976,8 +976,41 @@
   session->oscore_encryption = oscore_encryption;
   coap_delete_pdu_lkd(err_pdu);
   return;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Replay state of a Recipient Context before an incoming message advanced it.
+ * Restored when the message then fails verification (RFC 8613 8.2 Step 6 /
+ * 8.4 Step 5; Group OSCORE 7.2 / 7.4: "SHALL NOT update the Replay Window").
+ * Unlike oscore_roll_back_seq(), a saved value of 0 is restored as well and
+ * nothing is restored unless this message saved it.
+ */
+typedef struct {
+  uint64_t last_seq;
+  uint64_t sliding_window;
+  uint8_t initial_state;
+  uint8_t saved;
+} oscore_replay_state_t;
+
+static void
+oscore_replay_save(oscore_replay_state_t *st, const oscore_recipient_ctx_t *rcp) {
+  st->last_seq = rcp->last_seq;
+  st->sliding_window = rcp->sliding_window;
+  st->initial_state = rcp->initial_state;
+  st->saved = 1;
 }
 
+static void
+oscore_replay_restore(oscore_replay_state_t *st, oscore_recipient_ctx_t *rcp) {
+  if (!st->saved)
+    return;
+  rcp->last_seq = st->last_seq;
+  rcp->sliding_window = st->sliding_window;
+  rcp->initial_state = st->initial_state;
+  st->saved = 0;
+  coap_log_oscore("OSCORE: replay state restored after verification failure\n");
+}
+
 /* pdu contains incoming message with encrypted COSE ciphertext payload
  * function returns decrypted message
  * and verifies signature, if present
